ReSukiSU: accept the legacy SET_SEPOLICY ioctl ABI

ReSukiSU (575ea1a) changed KSU_IOCTL_SET_SEPOLICY to the batched format of
KernelSU v3.2.0: { u64 data_len; u64 data } pointing to a serialized payload.
ksud v3.1.x still sends { u64 cmd = 0; u64 arg = &FfiPolicy }, one rule per
call, so the kernel saw data_len == 0 and returned -EINVAL for every module
sepolicy.rule ("apply rule ... failed: Invalid argument (os error 22)").

Treat data_len == 0 as the legacy ABI: copy the FfiPolicy (cmd, subcmd,
sepol1..7 user pointers, NULL = ALL), re-encode it as a one-command batch in
kernel memory and run it through the existing batch parser and locking.
The batched format keeps working unchanged.

Apply inside the ReSukiSU checkout (kernel/KernelSU) with patch -p1.

